                        "entry_id": "ab71aadb-f621-310a-82c5-5fac0468475a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A birth defect in which the mandible is missing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7a44ebc-4fa8-474d-b599-f93b0e7402b8",
                                "sense_id": "3d8a181d-7e8d-310b-953e-486f9c4a687d",
                                "text": "When there is agnathia, instead of the inferior maxillary bone we find nothing but a kind of tubercle formed of skin, cellular tissue, fat, and some few muscular fibres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce66ac37-c6ca-4b97-b800-11b779db4da6",
                                "sense_id": "3d8a181d-7e8d-310b-953e-486f9c4a687d",
                                "text": "The lower jaw may be absent (agnathia)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31619bd8-3f17-4081-b89b-97c8527b54fb",
                                "sense_id": "3d8a181d-7e8d-310b-953e-486f9c4a687d",
                                "text": "As such, it is often accompanied by agnathia, a congenital absence of the mandible[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
